 "notes": "Dual comparator. Its outputs are open collector: each needs a pull-up resistor to give a high, typically 10 k. It only sinks, about 16 mA. Output low when IN- is above IN+.",
 "source": "TI LM393 datasheet",
 "spice": ".subckt CHIP_LM393 out1 inm1 inp1 gnd inp2 inm2 out2 vcc\nRin1 inp1 inm1 10Meg\nRin2 inp2 inm2 10Meg\nRs vcc gnd 5k\nBq1 out1 gnd I = v(out1,gnd)/30*lunes_step(v(inm1,gnd)-v(inp1,gnd),200)*lunes_step(v(vcc,gnd)-1.5,10)\nBq2 out2 gnd I = v(out2,gnd)/30*lunes_step(v(inm2,gnd)-v(inp2,gnd),200)*lunes_step(v(vcc,gnd)-1.5,10)\n.ends CHIP_LM393",
